# Models & Errors

Canonical owner for `archipy/models/`. Layer summary: `architecture-patterns.mdc`.

## Data-only layer

- Models contain **data structures only** — no I/O, no adapter calls, no business workflows.
- Prefer composition of DTOs/entities over logic in model methods (validators and formatting helpers on errors are OK when they stay pure).

## Layout

```
archipy/models/
├── entities/     # Persistence / domain entities (SQLAlchemy under entities/sqlalchemy/)
├── dtos/         # Pydantic BaseModel / BaseDTO transfer objects
├── errors/       # BaseError subclasses by domain
└── types/        # Enums and shared type aliases
```

## Entities

- Live under `entities/` (SQLAlchemy bases in `entities/sqlalchemy/`).
- Represent persisted or domain state — not transport payloads.
- Do not import adapters or helpers that perform I/O.

## DTOs

- Prefer subclassing `archipy.models.dtos.base_dtos.BaseDTO` (frozen, strip whitespace, `from_attributes`).
- Name by purpose: `*DTO`, search/query/result variants under domain folders (e.g. `dtos/redis/search/`).
- Keep DTOs free of infrastructure clients.

## Types

- Enums and shared aliases under `models/types/`.
- Export public types from `types/__init__.py` when part of the stable API.

## Errors (`BaseError`)

All custom errors subclass `archipy.models.errors.base_error.BaseError`.

Subclasses define class attributes:

- `code` — stable machine identifier (e.g. `INVALID_ARGUMENT`)
- `message_en` / `message_fa` — localized templates (`{variable}` placeholders OK)
- `http_status` / `grpc_status` — transport mapping on the error type

Organize new errors in the matching module:

| Module | Use for |
|---|---|
| `validation_errors.py` | Bad input, invalid arguments |
| `resource_errors.py` | Not found, conflicts |
| `auth_errors.py` | AuthN / AuthZ |
| `database_errors.py` | DB connectivity / integrity |
| `network_errors.py` | Remote network failures |
| `business_errors.py` | Domain rule violations |
| `system_errors.py` | Internal / config / unavailable |
| `keycloak_errors.py`, `temporal_errors.py`, … | Adapter-specific domains |

### Rules

- Prefer an existing error over inventing a near-duplicate.
- Pass context via constructor kwargs / `additional_data`, not by mutating `code` ad hoc.
- Adapters catch infrastructure exceptions and re-raise domain errors with `raise ... from e` (`adapter-conventions.mdc`).
- Transport (HTTP/gRPC) mapping belongs on the error class / helper utilities — not scattered in adapters.
- Export new public errors from `archipy/models/errors/__init__.py` when consumers need them.
